------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Provenance
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The decoder is an original implementation written from ATSC A/52:2018
(Digital Audio Compression (AC-3, E-AC-3) Standard), including its Annex E.
It is not a translation of, and does not derive from, any other AC-3 or
E-AC-3 decoder's source. The normative tables in src/tables.rs were
transcribed from the A/52:2018 PDF — the large ones extracted from its text
layer with an element-count check per table, the small ones typed in — and
each names the spec table and PDF page it came from. None was taken from
libavcodec or any other implementation.

The encoder is likewise an original implementation, written from the same
standard: its §8 (the informative description of an encoder) and the
normative syntax and decoding processes its output must satisfy, with
Annex E for E-AC-3. It is not a translation of, and does not derive from,
any other AC-3 or E-AC-3 encoder's source (libavcodec's ac3enc / eac3enc,
aften and Dolby's included: none was read). It reuses this crate's tables
and bit allocation routine. Its tests check its output against the
standard and decode it with this crate's decoder; no other encoder or
decoder is run by them.

The decoder is verified against libavcodec's decoder, used only as a black
box (the ffmpeg command-line tool, whose PCM output is compared); none of its
code is included or was consulted. The committed test stream in tests/data
was made by ffmpeg's AC-3 encoder, run the same way, and its reference PCM
by ffmpeg's decoder; they are tool output only.

